#N canvas 20 20 1600 1500 12;
#X text 20 20 c_voice -- one drum pad's sample \, played from memory. It loads samples/drums/NN.wav beside the patch at load \, NN its pad \, and plays it from the start on every hit \, so a hit cuts the one before as a one-shot pad on the 404 did. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 140 creation arg 1: its pad \, 1 to 16 \, and arg 2: c_kit's \$0 \, for the count of samples loaded and the throws to its delay and the reverb. inlet: a velocity \, 0 to 127 \, 0 ignored \, and vol <dB> and pitch <semitones> \, its track's volume and pitch from c_steps \, for the hits after them \, and its effects: drive \, tone \, dist (the mix) and char (the character \, 1 to 4) for its distortion \, delay (the level) and send <0-100>. outlet~: the sample \, mono \, its distortion mixed in. It throws the same at the delay's level to its e_delay \, \$2-d\$1 \, and at the send to e_verb \, \$2-verb. Once its sample is read \, it tells e_drive the sample's peak \, so a drive means the same on every pad., f 70;
#X obj 20 700 inlet;
#X obj 700 240 loadbang;
#X obj 700 280 t b b;
#X msg 900 320 0;
#X obj 700 320 f \$1;
#X obj 700 360 makefilename samples/drums/%02d.wav;
#X obj 700 400 list prepend dir 0;
#X obj 700 440 list trim;
#X obj 700 480 pdcontrol;
#X obj 700 520 t s s;
#X obj 850 600 symbol;
#X obj 700 560 file isfile;
