#X obj 20 1040 switch~;
#X obj 1200 240 array define \$0-smp;
#X text 1100 380 The path is the patch's own folder's \, so the Mac's main-dev.pd and the device find the samples the same way. file isfile first: a missing sample is no error \, just a silent pad \, and nothing reaches the console the deploy check reads., f 50;
#X text 600 1000 A hit: the level ramps to 0 in 2 ms \, the read jumps to the start 2 ms in \, then the level comes back in 1 ms and falls to 0 over the last 3 ms. The 2 ms keeps a retrigger from clicking. Velocity is 30 dB of range \, even steps in dB: 127 is 0 dB and 16 about -26 \, and the track's volume adds its own dB \, -30 to +6 \, to it. The track's pitch is the read's rate \, 2 to the power of semitones over 12: the read \, the level's fall and switch~ all take the sample's length over the rate \, so a pitch is worked out once \, when it arrives \, and both take effect at the next hit., f 50;
#X text 20 1100 switch~ keeps a voice's DSP off except while it sounds: a voice costs about 0.65% of the Organelle's core while on (Reference \, Organelle page). e_drive \, the distortion \, has a switch~ of its own \, on while its mix is above 0 \, and so does taps \, while the delay's level or the send is: inside this one \, each runs only while the voice sounds., f 34;
#X obj 20 730 route float vol pitch;
#X obj 190 770 s \$0-vol;
#X obj 300 770 s \$0-pitch;
#X obj 640 845 r \$0-vol;
#X obj 1150 640 r \$0-pitch;
#X obj 1150 680 t b f;
#X obj 1150 720 f;
